From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackParrot Context Resume Experiment <noreply@example.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sched: trigger BlackParrot shared instruction replay

Start the machine-configured, address-free shared instruction prefix only after
the scheduler selects a different task. The custom supervisor CSR is specific
to the experimental BlackParrot platform; other architectures compile no
instruction.
---
 kernel/sched/core.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/core.c b/kernel/sched/core.c
index 802551e00000..802551e00001 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/core.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/core.c
@@ -6648,6 +6648,13 @@ static void __sched notrace __schedule(unsigned int sched_mode)
 #endif
 
 	if (likely(prev != next)) {
+#ifdef CONFIG_RISCV
+		/* Physical prefix contents are machine-owned. Launch only for an
+		 * actual task change so failed selections do not replay the table.
+		 */
+		asm volatile("csrw 0x5c0, zero" ::: "memory");
+#endif
+
 		rq->nr_switches++;
 		/*
 		 * RCU users of rcu_dereference(rq->curr) may not see
-- 
2.34.1
